      • Opaque white (#FFFFFF) = visible icon
      • Transparent = invisible background
      • The OS applies its own tint color (usually white on dark backgrounds)
    
    This version removes all shading/gradient paths for a clean, flat appearance
    that works correctly as a notification icon on all Android versions.
-->
